+# POWER HOME AI COACH — review before any production deployment
+
+Baseline: verified `power-home-94.0.0.tar.gz`, SHA256 `42f639cea7a8b76970f17e806e37de6dca780ce59dc96f572e9203debdc8ca3b` and `install-9400.sh`. The GitHub root contains older partial source files; the verified full release archive is the baseline. This branch contains a full source archive and a readable patch against that release. It is NOT a separate application.
+
+## Architecture
+
+Next.js 16 / React 19 / TypeScript, existing SQLite adapter and coach/student session authentication, existing encrypted-payload helper, exercise/food bank, manual builder and PDF renderer. No new runtime dependency: the installed Zod package exposes its v4 entrypoint for Structured Outputs. Existing version94 raw-db initializer is unchanged.
+
+Coach menu → AI Coach → choose engines/style/athlete constraints → explicit consent gate and selected references/photos → fixed OpenAI Responses endpoint, `store:false`, no tools, no automatic retries → strict schema plus business-rule validation → encrypted draft and append-only revisions → explicit coach approval of the current revision → transfer selected sections to the EXISTING manual builder → edit/save/send through the existing coach publication action. The AI endpoint does not call program-delivery, change coach_states, send a student message or auto-publish a plan.
+
+**Manual programming remains fully available, even with no API key, no migration, a denied student consent or API outage.** AI transfer changes only selected training/nutrition/supplement sections; medication sections and unselected content stay intact. Both training/rest meal sets are retained in the draft; coach explicitly chooses which meal set to transfer. The existing v94 ClientPlan supports one meal schedule, so automatic switching between two daily schedules is deliberately not introduced.
+
+Three modes: independent rejects archive and golden IDs; coach/hybrid send only selected, owner-scoped sample plans. Names/medical profiles/photos are not included in style references; references are reduced to exercise IDs, sets/reps/rest/techniques and structured foods. Legacy free-text meals are not mined because they may contain private notes. Golden templates/rules are saved only from an approved version and included in generation only when explicitly selected.
+
+Split, method and technique are separate typed records. Custom systems have an explicit approved flag; generation rejects pending systems and type mismatches. Manual per-day split titles remain coach-controlled. The rotating three-on/one-off split can be described and reviewed, but v94's calendar assignment remains manual; this version does not silently turn a rolling cycle into a fixed weekly schedule.
+
+Training validation checks permitted/forbidden/required catalog IDs, exact session count/day titles, max working sets, coach RIR/RPE/rest, allowed techniques, and the weekly frequency/set targets of up to three priority muscles, using the existing primary-muscle classifier. Secondary muscle contributions are not claimed as measured volume. Equipment suitability is narrowed by the coach's explicitly allowed exercise list; free-text equipment does not pretend to be an exhaustive equipment ontology.
+
+Nutrition uses an editable Mifflin–St Jeor baseline, activity factor, explicit calorie delta/override, protein/fat per kg, and residual carbs. The model receives the estimates and selected catalog macros. Server calculates returned nutrients from trusted food IDs/grams, checks calorie/protein/fat/carb tolerances and approximate alternatives, and preserves raw/cooked catalog state. Weight trend and food budget are inputs for explanatory suggestions; there is no verified food-price feed or automatic trend-based calorie publication.
+
+Supplements intentionally start with only creatine monohydrate and protein powder. Adult-only requests, reviewed safety information, and no reported medication/medical/injury/allergy/digestive concerns are required for dose suggestions. Otherwise an empty supplement list and professional review are required. Creatine is capped at5g/day; powder at40g/day and only with a recorded dietary protein shortfall. Product protein concentration and individual clinical suitability still require review. This is a conservative safety gate, NOT a complete drug-interaction checker or clinical prescribing system. No medication/hormone/steroid/stimulant protocols are supported in AI outputs. Existing manual medication functions are unchanged.
+
+Visual requests accept only selected front/back/side photos belonging to that athlete, at most6, <=1MB each and3MB total. Existing protected weekly and archived-body photo storage is reused. No external URL fetching or identity/diagnosis/body-fat measurement tools. Qualitative observations have low/moderate confidence and limitations; numeric measurements from image observations are rejected. Image observations remain draft suggestions requiring human review.
+
+## Consent, privacy and security
+
+Student-owned `GET/PUT /api/student/ai-consent` records current disclosure version and separate data/photo/medical grants with a timestamped audit trail. Missing or revoked grants stop NEW transmissions. The grant is rechecked immediately before the provider call. Revocation cannot retract a request already sent. `store:false` is not a guarantee of zero retention for provider abuse monitoring; disclosure says this explicitly. No real student data or photos were sent during development/testing.
+
+Coach routes require the existing coach session and same-origin writes. Client ownership, reference ownership, photo ownership, IDs, output schema, system approval and revision/hash checks are server-side. No API key readback, browser storage, GitHub inclusion or content logging. No model tools execute commands or fetch arbitrary URLs. Untrusted reference/image/text instructions are isolated as data; allowlists and output validation restrict damage, but prompt injection cannot be proven impossible. A coach must review every result.
+
+Failures keep prior drafts. Provider rejection/refusal/invalid output never publishes. Actual API token usage and cached tokens, provider response/request IDs, rate snapshot and calculated USD are recorded when available. Dollar values are calculated from **operator-confirmed rates**, not a billing-provider invoice integration; they must be reconciled against the actual invoice. Unknown network outcomes retain a conservative budget reservation, block retries/concurrent calls, and require explicit operator invoice reconciliation. No fake zero-cost reporting. Monthly default50attempts includes regeneration/failures; total USD cap is separately configurable. Conservative image reservations may reject a request even when its eventual cost would be lower.
+
+## Database and rollback
+
+Additive, opt-in SQL in `migrations/ai-coach-up.sql`: `ai_consents`, `ai_consent_events`, `ai_systems`, `ai_settings`, `ai_jobs`, `ai_drafts`, `ai_draft_versions`, `ai_golden_rules`. Sensitive draft/system/golden payloads reuse encryption. Baseline tables and raw-db migration logic are untouched. `AI_COACH_SCHEMA=1` enables lazy idempotent schema creation only in AI endpoints; leave it unset on production until an approved deployment/migration plan exists.
+
+For rollback: first disable AI (`AI_COACH_SCHEMA=0`), back up the database and export required AI audit/history; run `migrations/ai-coach-down.sql` ONLY on the intended copy. Down SQL deletes AI records, so it is never auto-run. Baseline manual programs, accounts and coach state are preserved. In production, prefer disabling the module and keeping audit tables rather than dropping them.
+
+## Local-only testing and API setup
+
+Use a fresh directory for APP_DATA_DIR; NEVER mount/copy a live credentials file or point this checkout at the production database. Install exact package-lock dependencies. Node22.13+ is required.
+
+```bash
+APP_DATA_DIR=/tmp/power-home-ai-dev AI_COACH_SCHEMA=1 npm run dev
+npm run build
+node --test tests/*.test.mjs
+```
+
+The test suite creates its own disposable SQLite directory and injects a fake provider. It does not consume paid API credit. The UI defaults to disabled until configuration and consent are present.
+
+For an explicitly authorized real API smoke test, set `OPENAI_API_KEY` and `AI_COACH_MODEL` ONLY as server environment variables/secret manager values. Never prefix them NEXT_PUBLIC, put keys in query strings, commit them, or share them in chat. Choose a model supporting Responses vision + Structured Outputs; there is no hard-coded paid model. Optional `AI_COACH_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` is clamped1000–16000. Coach settings must explicitly enable AI, match the configured model/rate model, confirm current token prices (including cached input), record the rate-check date, set monthly request/USD limits, and obtain the student's grants. Start with synthetic data and a small cap. ChatGPT Plus does not provide API credit.
+
+No production deployment script is included or invoked for this AI change. No main merge is authorized.
+
+## External documentation used
+
+- OpenAI quickstart: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/quickstart
+- Structured Outputs: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/structured-outputs
+- Responses: https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/responses/methods/create
+- Vision: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/images-vision
+- ISSN creatine position: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5469049/
+- ISSN protein position: https://doi.org/10.1186/s12970-017-0177-8
+
+Remaining review limits: no real-provider quality/latency/billing smoke test, no exhaustive medical interaction database, and no authenticated mobile/Safari visual run yet. This must be treated as an implementation for review, not as a claim of clinically validated or production-approved AI.
